Let's describe what we're talking about.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.600
Yeah, go into it.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:27.680
Go for it. So basically what Mike and I both experienced, and maybe Joe, Joe, did you experience this

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.760
too? If we're talking about the same thing, once you explain it, I'll confirm that that was what

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.660
I experienced. Okay.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:40.880
Um, basically, yeah, there's eight different directions you can fire in, and like many games

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:47.880
that you can fire in eight different directions, like, that it feels like you always have to

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.260
be firing in the direction that you're moving.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:57.280
But once you start holding the button down, then you realize that you can continue firing

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.540
in the original direction and move freely.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.540
Yeah, I did experience that exactly as well.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:09.160
Okay. It's crazy that that could be an issue that all three of us would run into not talk about

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.380
until the day of the episode.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.100
But I'm glad we all were able to overcome it.

