very frustrated. Every time I would, you know, obviously try and go in one direction, I would turn that

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.620
direction. And then, you know, and I kept dying, and I was doing it a lot.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:21.140
And then, like, after a while, I kind of stopped noticing it.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.040
And then a while later, it just suddenly dawned on me, like, oh, it hasn't been happening

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.940
anymore. Because I just slowly, just naturally started holding down the button as things got harder.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.680
And I was like, I don't remember when that stopped.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.620
But then I, like, realized, oh, okay, this game's not so bad anymore.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.240
Like, but I don't remember the moment when I realized it just slowly started to happen

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:46.220
for me. And what's funny about that very first group of enemies is that they kind of home into

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:51.860
you from, you know, first they're spread out, and then they are closing in on you.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.260
So there isn't really a way to avoid them.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.860
You kind of have to shoot them to get past them, because you're in a narrow space, and

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.600
the enemies are heading directly towards you.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:08.280
So you either have the option of being, like, a very skilled shooter, and while moving, also,

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.960
like, having twitch-like reflexes to go back into shooting straight on and taking out the

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.820
next variable line before moving in another position and shooting that particular enemy

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.020
down. Like, that requires some sharp shooting.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:26.680
Instead, to Sean's mention, is that, like, by holding down the button, something that

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:34.040
you would usually think would fire one single shot, it now fires shots over and over and

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.980
over again. Not in, like, a turbo sense, but definitely in an unexpected way.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:45.360
And once you figure that out, all of a sudden, the multiple direction shooting really frees up

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:51.400
this game and makes it really cool and kind of reminds me of, you know, Section Z, a game

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:56.780
where the A and B button were being used for the A button would shoot to the right and the

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:58.140
B button would shoot to the left.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:03.100
So as they are on the controller, it would make sense, and you would be able to switch on

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:09.980
the fly. Here, you're able to shoot in all cardinal directions and move freely around the screen

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:15.980
at the same time. And I know that doesn't sound revolutionary, but because it is eight directions, it certainly

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:21.520
gives you more power than any horizontal or vertical shmup did in the past, where you're

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:26.800
mostly just shooting a linear line until you get power-ups that give you spreads and the

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:32.080
like. Yeah, it solves this issue that I've had with a bunch of other shmups where, like, as soon

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.340
as you pass something, it's just still a threat behind you, but you can't do anything

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:41.300
about it. And yeah, I think Section Z did that too, but this also gives you the option to shoot

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:46.220
up or down, and it, you know, you do start to notice that, like, some of the enemies are

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:49.680
designed in a way where you gotta think, like, oh, I have to get beneath this thing and shoot

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.100
up at it, or, you know, get around its armor.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.140
So at least it wasn't just, like, a function, but it's like, oh, the game was somewhat designed

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:05.220
around it too. Yeah, it also just sort of feels cool to, like, get at, like, a diagonal angle to get maybe,

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:12.180
like, a turret than in any other shmup would be almost impossible to hit before you, like,

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:18.240
get to a certain point in the scroll and just sort of just snipe it, you know, just sort

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.520
of drift in and snipe it, you know?

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:21.900
It feels cool.

