00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:05.800
So this way you make sure that you get the one that you're in need of to upgrade.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:14.900
So, um, you know, I, I, I wonder if they could have, um, either made them not so powerful,

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:19.660
I guess, or if they could have just focused on like making it so this way you don't feel

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.960
fully upgraded so early on.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:32.180
Yeah. I, I guess the, the counter is every time you collect a, a pickup that is not the one

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:39.940
that you last picked up, your, your firing, uh, pattern, I guess changes entirely.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:47.580
Like there's only, like, I couldn't really get a perfect handle on what was going on because

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:52.800
it seems that if you have everything maxed out, you get this like great omnidirectional

00:17:52.800 --> 00:18:01.280
fire, um, that you can either have mostly going into the corners or mostly going, uh, like

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.280
in a cross pattern.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:08.520
But if you're, if you're picking them up and you're not fully maxed out, you, you're either

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:16.880
getting sort of a spread with the, uh, the rings or just that, uh, that straight on shot

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.000
with. Right. It's whatever you picked up last.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:26.040
Yeah. So I figure like, it's not that none of them are perfect and it's more so you're sort of

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:34.440
switching between near at the later, like numbers of each power up, uh, you're just sort of picking

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:35.980
what kind of fire you want.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:40.380
And it's not really getting fully upgraded until you've pretty much maxed everything out.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:47.600
In addition, players can, uh, uh, fire bombs, which they have a limited supply of that, um,

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.860
you know, destroy the enemies on screen.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:55.720
But interestingly, uh, maybe in a first, these don't do any damage to the bosses.

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:00.900
So they are encouraged to be used in the actual stage rather than like, Whoa, well, I'm just

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.280
going to save my bombs for the big boss fight.

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:04.720
Uh, won't do you any good here.

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:07.200
Better make sure you use them when you need them.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:12.420
Yeah. I don't think that's the necessarily the best solution, but I do sort of appreciate it

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:16.720
actually, because I, I find myself in games like this that have like, you know, if it's

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:22.360
like a shmup and it has difficult boss battles, I find myself like discouraged from using

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.980
the, the power-ups when I really need them.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:30.500
