00:32:21.180 --> 00:32:23.000
But not on the Essential Games list.

00:32:23.340 --> 00:32:34.180
Sean? Yeah, I think mechanically, this is probably one of the best feeling shmups to play.

00:32:34.580 --> 00:32:45.460
And it's actually the second shmup in a row that is broken with that tired idea that shmups are just a template

00:32:45.460 --> 00:32:50.240
that lazy games just get, you know, churned out.

00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:55.180
I'm pleasantly surprised with the variety of shmup that we've been getting recently.

00:32:55.460 --> 00:32:57.800
But at the end of the day, it is still a shmup.

00:32:57.800 --> 00:33:10.600
And a lot of where these games sort of separate from the pack is their vibe and the aesthetic.

00:33:11.100 --> 00:33:12.520
And I just didn't...

00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:15.060
This game doesn't have a lot of style.

00:33:15.340 --> 00:33:19.060
It has cool boss fights, and I really like the base mechanics.

00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:22.160
But the backgrounds are kind of blah.

00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:24.640
The enemies are kind of blah.

00:33:25.360 --> 00:33:27.720
And the story is...

00:33:27.720 --> 00:33:30.480
That was not even thought about.

00:33:31.340 --> 00:33:33.540
Even as like a fun little...

00:33:33.540 --> 00:33:37.720
Like we made Burai fun with whatever we were talking about.

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:41.620
The game didn't. So I agree.

00:33:41.620 --> 00:33:43.280
This is definitely a play it.

00:33:43.780 --> 00:33:44.920
But not essential.

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:48.020
I'll echo you on the mechanics there.

00:33:48.100 --> 00:33:52.740
I think that the mechanics were a highlight of this game.

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:55.180
It was... I mean, really just in the fact...

00:33:55.180 --> 00:33:56.500
Like it sounds so simple.

00:33:56.640 --> 00:33:58.480
But in the fact that you can face any direction.

00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:01.160
Changes up the way you think about this shmup.

00:34:01.280 --> 00:34:02.380
Like compared to other things.

00:34:02.500 --> 00:34:05.800
And it really... It was a breath of fresh air in that sense.

00:34:06.380 --> 00:34:08.120
But as far as like the rest of the game.

00:34:08.340 --> 00:34:09.520
I mean, I'll be honest.

00:34:09.780 --> 00:34:12.120
You could probably take any...

00:34:12.120 --> 00:34:16.180
Like one of a dozen or so other essential votes.

00:34:16.340 --> 00:34:17.560
That I've done for other shmups.

00:34:17.720 --> 00:34:18.680
And like paste it here.

00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:20.880
And it's... And it's gonna be the same thing.

00:34:20.980 --> 00:34:22.040
Like it didn't blow me away.

00:34:22.160 --> 00:34:23.380
It didn't do anything that like...

00:34:24.360 --> 00:34:26.060
Stands out from the rest.

00:34:26.300 --> 00:34:27.260
Other than that mechanic.

00:34:27.460 --> 00:34:29.040
Which I don't think is enough.

00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:30.500
For me to be like, yes.

00:34:30.580 --> 00:34:31.440
This is a must play.

00:34:31.780 --> 00:34:33.640
So I'm going to also say...

00:34:33.640 --> 00:34:34.900
No. Not an essential game.

00:34:34.900 --> 00:34:37.700
And so therefore it won't be on the essential games list.

00:34:37.860 --> 00:34:38.700
But that's okay.

00:34:39.120 --> 00:34:41.380
Every game gets a chance at the essential games list.

00:34:41.620 --> 00:34:42.520
Like our next game.

00:34:42.780 --> 00:34:43.700
Codename Viper.

00:34:44.720 --> 00:34:46.360
Codename colon Viper.

00:34:46.640 --> 00:34:49.500
So this way you know that his codename is Viper.

00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:51.000
Oh, good.

00:34:52.500 --> 00:34:53.700
So when it says...

00:34:53.700 --> 00:34:55.940
It's spelled out. Codename colon Viper.

00:34:56.400 --> 00:34:58.300
The colon is spelled out.

00:34:58.460 --> 00:34:59.800
Yeah. It's not two dots.

00:35:00.360 --> 00:35:02.500
Yeah. Oh, maybe it's a colon Viper.

00:35:03.140 --> 00:35:04.180
That's what I was thinking.

00:35:04.460 --> 00:35:07.100
Dude, it's like some kind of weird parasite that you have to...

00:35:07.100 --> 00:35:08.560
I like that idea.

00:35:08.880 --> 00:35:10.080
It's a Capcom game.

00:35:10.080 --> 00:35:11.260
So we like their stuff.

00:35:11.520 --> 00:35:14.060
Apparently it's also an Arc System Works game.

00:35:14.260 --> 00:35:15.840
Which is... They were making games back then.

00:35:15.920 --> 00:35:18.460
That's crazy. This will be our first Arc System Works game.

00:35:18.520 --> 00:35:21.240
So that's cool. These are the guys who make Dragon Ball Fighters.

00:35:21.520 --> 00:35:22.860
Right? Oh.

00:35:22.860 --> 00:35:24.200
And the BlazBlue games.

00:35:24.200 --> 00:35:25.000
I don't know. All that stuff.

00:35:25.600 --> 00:35:26.420
Maybe. Interesting.

00:35:26.600 --> 00:35:27.900
Guys, they make beautiful...

00:35:27.900 --> 00:35:30.260
They make the most beautiful fighting games I've ever seen.

00:35:31.300 --> 00:35:35.520
Anyway, if that's not your cup of tea, the following week we'll be playing Conflict.

00:35:35.880 --> 00:35:37.100
That's what the game's called.

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:38.940
Sounds like a board game, honestly.

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:43.480
It's just funny because it's like, oh, any good story or game needs a conflict.

00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:47.340
It's like they might as well just call it like protagonist fights antagonist.

00:35:47.940 --> 00:35:51.500
And that's by Vic Takai, who we've played many of his games.

00:35:52.020 --> 00:35:54.100
Good old Vic. Friend of the show, Vic Vitae.

00:35:57.040 --> 00:36:02.600
Also, trying to ask questions, but this time I'll maybe try and relate it to the episode.

00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:05.020
You know, we played a lot of shmups.

00:36:05.260 --> 00:36:13.320
So what's a franchise that you dig that you would like to see a shmup iteration into their franchise?

00:36:13.820 --> 00:36:14.840
Ratchet and Clank.

00:36:15.300 --> 00:36:17.140
A Ratchet and Clank shmup.

00:36:17.260 --> 00:36:21.000
Could you tell me maybe like a power-up or two or something that they would do?

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:27.560
Yeah, I mean, they have so many interesting gadgets and weapons that don't just do like...

00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:35.460
They're good at coming up with things that aren't just like, this one explodes with a blast radius and this one is a shotgun and whatever.

00:36:35.660 --> 00:36:37.160
It's like they have unique things.

00:36:37.160 --> 00:36:39.160
It's like, this one sucks enemies into it.

00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:41.620
One of them turns people into flaming ducks.

00:36:42.020 --> 00:36:44.580
You know, like all kinds of different like...

00:36:44.580 --> 00:36:47.660
You know, this weapon makes people dance.

00:36:47.900 --> 00:36:53.000
You know, I think that could be interesting in a shmup format.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:56.940
And yeah, in one of the Ratchet and Clank's there's a weapon that makes any enemy in the game dance.

00:36:57.180 --> 00:37:04.540
Every single enemy in the game has, in case needed, their own animation for like the way that they would dance.

00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:06.660
So like, you know, that could be cool.

00:37:06.960 --> 00:37:08.600
Out of the park baseball.

00:37:09.840 --> 00:37:11.440
But the shmup version.

00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:23.420
And is that just like, you know, you're just kind of like tinkering with different like spaceships stats and sending them out onto the battlefield.

00:37:23.520 --> 00:37:27.880
And you're just like reviewing the battle reports afterwards.

00:37:28.340 --> 00:37:29.660
Oh, you know what? All right.

00:37:29.740 --> 00:37:31.380
No, not out of the park baseball then.

00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:32.760
Just like any kind of baseball.

00:37:32.980 --> 00:37:34.640
I just want a baseball themed shmup.

00:37:34.720 --> 00:37:36.000
I want to know how they do it.

00:37:37.420 --> 00:37:38.920
What would you be shooting?

00:37:39.100 --> 00:37:39.920
Is it baseballs?

00:37:39.980 --> 00:37:44.120
Is it bats? You're the pitcher shooting baseballs at batters.

00:37:44.180 --> 00:37:50.120
And if they make contact, then you have to catch the balls and become the fielder.

00:37:50.360 --> 00:37:53.640
But otherwise, if they swing and miss, they blow up.

00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:55.780
All right. You just developed the game for me.

00:37:55.960 --> 00:38:00.660
There you go. I'll always help you out because out of the park baseball was a reach.

00:38:02.460 --> 00:38:03.420
You're a reach.

00:38:03.580 --> 00:38:09.260
My answer may be a little more like in the realm of things that are possible.

00:38:09.260 --> 00:38:16.500
I feel like Kirby has had some shmup-ish levels where like, you know, because he's already like he always puffs up.

00:38:16.720 --> 00:38:18.680
And then he already has when he's puffed up.

00:38:18.840 --> 00:38:25.400
He has the ability to blow out whatever air he's sucked in as one attack for an enemy.

00:38:25.400 --> 00:38:28.560
But imagine if he just had like, he was permanently inflated.

00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:29.960
And that's like the plot of it.

00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:32.400
It's called Kirby's Permanent Inflation.

00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:36.620
And I mean, they did it with Sonic, right?

00:38:36.880 --> 00:38:39.260
Yeah. They did it with Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:38:39.820 --> 00:38:42.720
Isn't that actually like a level in Kirby's Dream Land?

00:38:43.000 --> 00:38:46.820
I feel like it was like, it's on a small way.

00:38:47.260 --> 00:38:48.460
It's already been done.

00:38:48.580 --> 00:38:52.780
But now imagine it's like a whole game with like, you know, also riding.

00:38:53.060 --> 00:38:55.440
You know, he rides those stars from level to level.

00:38:55.600 --> 00:38:58.680
It's like a little bit of like Kirby's air ride thing going on.

00:38:58.680 --> 00:39:03.820
And your power-ups can be like sucking in enemies and then like getting their power-up.

00:39:04.700 --> 00:39:07.040
Absolutely. I mean, that's the Kirby thing.

00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:08.720
Yeah. All right.

00:39:09.060 --> 00:39:11.460
So someone call Sakurai.

00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:13.800
We figured out his next Kirby game.

00:39:13.980 --> 00:39:18.880
He did make an on-rails Kid Icarus, which is another thing we were talking about today, right?

00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:20.920
Yeah. It's a great game.

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:22.280
Kid Icarus Uprising.

00:39:23.400 --> 00:39:26.400
Great game. Tough game to play on that system, though.

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:28.120
That's the 3DS game, right?

00:39:28.120 --> 00:39:34.360
Yeah, yeah. You need to have like that weird attachment that gives you the second analog stick to really make it a good game.

00:39:34.460 --> 00:40:01.820
But whatever. I like the 3DS. Thank you.
